    "panels": [
      {
        "text": "**Autopilot** is when AI is doing a larger part of the work for you, like turning a wireframe, content plan, or style guide into a webpage. That can be useful, but it does not mean you stop paying attention. A flight plan helps the plane know where to go, but the pilot still watches the route, checks for problems, and takes control when needed. In designing and building a website, responsible autopilot means reviewing what AI creates, checking that it matches your audience and purpose, and making adjustments before you call the work finished.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/0a3a3eca5be16736edae6e9ea154bc35-iste_autopilot.png",
